wordexp's WRDE_NOCMD check reads the words as the shell will (musl's scans for characters, so it took a { or } in
${x-{}, a ( in $((...)) or a quoted one for an operator, and missed a command substitution in $(( ) ...)): quotes,
${...} words, quoted as the expansion is except a pattern's, $((...)), $'...', comments and line continuations.
WRDE_UNDEF is set -u, and the shell parses the words before it expands them, writing a marker in between, so a
syntax error (no marker) is told from an expansion that failed (no words after it), WRDE_BADVAL with WRDE_UNDEF.

